["M009",13,"The declaration is the additive theorem generated by the displayed to_additive annotation, not the primed multiplicative theorem. Its complete native type requires only a topological domain and seminormed additive group, compact set and continuity on that set. The existential real bound and every-point-on-the-set quantifier are faithfully retained, with no nonempty-set requirement.",["Mathlib/Analysis/Normed/Group/Bounded.lean:27-30","Mathlib/Analysis/Normed/Group/Bounded.lean:96-100"]],
["M010",14,"The finite-index product-Lebesgue box formula is faithfully restated for arbitrary real endpoint families: volume(Icc a b)=∏i ENNReal.ofReal(b_i−a_i). Fintype is explicit, and the nonnegative-part interpretation of ofReal preserves reversed and degenerate intervals rather than assuming ordered endpoints.",["Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Measure/Lebesgue/Basic.lean:48-50","Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Measure/Lebesgue/Basic.lean:237-248"]],
["M011",15,"The restatement retains finite index type, measurable coordinate spaces, sigma-finiteness of every measure and a decidable predicate. The equivalence is exactly restriction to the positive and negative predicate subtypes, and the target product measures are in that order. The source definition and its explicit inverse confirm that this is a measurable equivalence; no singleton-to-real specialization is hidden in M011 (that is addressed separately by M017).",["Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Constructions/Pi.lean:712-727","Mathlib/MeasureTheory/MeasurableSpace/Embedding.lean:572-577","Mathlib/Logic/Equiv/Prod.lean:465-475"]],
["M012",16,"The finite-sum integral statement retains the arbitrary finite index set, measurable space/measure, normed additive commutative real normed codomain and integrability of each member indexed by that set. The two ∑ i∈s forms are the native finite sum, not an iterated arbitrary-series claim. The cached report is explicitly mapped from original_source_id M001 to current sources.M012; its unchanged stdout M001 marker names MeasureTheory.integral_finsetSum and exactly the same signature/axioms. This is disclosed metadata reuse, not a fresh query.",["Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Integral/Bochner/Basic.lean:246-251","signature-evidence.json#/M012/0/metadata_reuse","signature-evidence.json#/M012/0/result/stdout"]],
