["M014",18,"The statement includes the full normed division ring, normed additive commutative real normed codomain, Module, NormSMulClass and SMulCommClass ℝ 𝕜 G assumptions. NormSMulClass is the native exact norm-multiplication requirement, not merely bounded scalar multiplication. The unrestricted integrand and absence of an integrability premise faithfully match the total Bochner integral theorem.",["Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Integral/Bochner/Basic.lean:150-159","Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Integral/Bochner/Basic.lean:270-278","Mathlib/Analysis/Normed/MulAction.lean:93-99"]],
["M016",25,"The full type requires a measure-preserving map and a measurable embedding, in addition to both measurable spaces/measures and the real normed additive commutative codomain. Both map assumptions are explicit in the restatement; measure-preserving means measurable with pushforward equal to the target measure. The identity's direction and unrestricted total-integral meaning agree with native integral_comp. No omitted integrability or sigma-finiteness hypothesis is present.",["Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Integral/Bochner/Basic.lean:1077-1084","Mathlib/Dynamics/Ergodic/MeasurePreserving.lean:43-48"]],
